  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating and comparing the variances of the lotteries, with a preference for the lower variance. The individual did not consider variance or any related concept (such as risk spread or outcome stability). Instead, the individual focused on the higher payoff under the assumption of equal probabilities. There is no overlap in the information used (variance vs. outcome size and perceived probability equality), and the justification (choosing the higher gain) does not align with the rule of minimizing variance. Therefore, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
